#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:3
msgid "Running applications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:5
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` downloads and runs a Python application in a one-time, "
"temporary environment, then leaves your system untouched. Reach for it to "
"scaffold a new project, check an app's help text, or try a tool without "
"committing to an install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:11
msgid "Basic usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:13
msgid "$ pipx run pycowsay moo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:17
msgid ""
"pipx installs the package in an isolated, temporary directory and invokes "
"the app:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:19
msgid ""
"$ pipx run pycowsay moo\n"
"  ---\n"
"< moo >\n"
"  ---\n"
"   \\   ^__^\n"
"    \\  (oo)\\_______\n"
"       (__)\\       )\\/\\\n"
"           ||----w |\n"
"           ||     ||"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:31
msgid "Arguments after the app name pass straight through to it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:33
msgid "$ pipx run pycowsay these arguments all go to pycowsay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:39
msgid "Ambiguous arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:41
msgid ""
"pipx can swallow an argument meant for the app when it looks like one of "
"pipx's own options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:43
msgid ""
"$ pipx run pycowsay --py\n"
"pipx run: error: ambiguous option: --py could match --python-args, --"
"pypackages, --python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:48
msgid "Put ``--`` before the app name to forward everything after it verbatim:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:50
msgid "$ pipx run -- pycowsay --py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:56
msgid "When the app name differs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:58
msgid ""
"Some packages expose an app under a different name, or expose several. Use "
"``--spec`` to name the package and the app separately:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:61
msgid "$ pipx run --spec PACKAGE APP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:65
msgid ""
"`esptool <https://github.com/espressif/esptool>`_, for example, lists its "
"executables when you guess wrong:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:67
msgid ""
"$ pipx run esptool\n"
"'esptool' executable script not found in package 'esptool'.\n"
"Available executable scripts:\n"
"    esptool.py - usage: 'pipx run --spec esptool esptool.py [arguments?]'\n"
"    espefuse.py - usage: 'pipx run --spec esptool espefuse.py [arguments?]'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:75
msgid "Run the one you want with ``--spec``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:77
msgid "$ pipx run --spec esptool esptool.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:81
msgid ""
"Package authors can remove this requirement by declaring a :doc:`pipx.run "
"entry point <../explanation/making-packages-compatible>` in their metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:88
msgid "Run cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:90
msgid ""
"pipx caches each ``pipx run`` environment for a few days so repeated runs "
"start instantly. After the cache expires, the next run fetches the latest "
"version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:109
msgid ""
"Force a rebuild before the cache expires with ``--refresh``, which replaces "
"that app's cached environment and keeps the replacement:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:112
msgid "$ pipx run --refresh APP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:116
msgid ""
"``--no-cache`` also rebuilds, but marks the new environment for cleanup by a "
"later run. The two options are mutually exclusive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:119
msgid "Inspect or clear every cached run environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:121
msgid ""
"$ pipx cache dir\n"
"$ pipx cache purge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:126
msgid ""
"For how pipx decides what to cache and when, see :doc:`How pipx works <../"
"explanation/how-pipx-works>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:130
msgid "Learn more"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/run-applications.rst:132
msgid ""
":doc:`Use the uv backend <../how-to/use-uv-backend>`: run with uv, which "
"keeps its own ephemeral cache."
msgstr ""

